<title>USA: U.S. soybean export sales lowest since start of yr.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean export sales lowest since start of yr.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said net U.S. soybean export sales in the week ended May 8 were at the lowest level since the start of the year.</p>
<p>In its weekly export sales report, USDA said net soybean sales dipped to 141,200 tonnes, off 41 percent from the previous week and 54 percent from the four-week average, and the lowest since 81,600 tonnes in the week ended January 2.</p>
<p>Analysts had been expecting soybean exports to tumble in the week, sapped by competition from Argentina and Brazil. Trade estimates were for 100,000 to 200,000 tonnes.</p>
